The ID scroll is the cheapest by far. It's also the second most
common.

Use-identifying rings is tricky. Without spoiling much, *don't* put on
cursed ones, and stay *far* away from powerful peacefuls such as
shopkeepers or priests. The rest typically aren't bad. If you avoid
the latter, the worst that can happen is rapidly increased hunger.

And if you don't know how to identify cursed stuff, it's in the
guidebook: drop your stuff on an altar and watch what happens.

As for food, eat fresh corpses whenever you're not satiated, or play
as an archaeologist to use their starting tinning kit.


